-        string api_token_hash
-        bool is_active
-        datetime last_seen_at
-    }
-```
-
-## Main Relationships
-
-| Relationship | Cardinality | Business Rule |
-| ------------ | ----------- | ------------- |
-| `entities` → `billing_accounts` | 1 : 0..1 | Financial data isolated; not loaded with entity (optional in MVP) |
-| `billing_accounts` → `subscriptions` | 1 : 1 | One subscription per entity; history in `payments` |
-| `payment_options` → `subscriptions` | 1 : 1 | Defines payment method (cycle, method, discount) |
-| `subscriptions` → `payments` | 1 : N | Individual charges; status synced with Asaas |
-| `entities` → `entity_memberships` | 1 : N | User operates within one entity (see cardinality note) |
-| `entities` → `owner` (`entity_memberships`) | 1 : 1 | Invariant: exactly one owner per entity (via `owner_membership_id`) |
-| `entity_memberships.role` | enum | `admin`, `owner`, `employee` — billing only for owner |
-| `plans` → limits | — | `max_users`, `max_queues` |
-| `queue_access` | join 1:N/1:N | Employee: granular permissions per queue |
-| `queues` → `tickets` | 1 : N | Ticket belongs to **one** queue; ordering by `priority` (desc) + `issued_at` (asc) |
-| `users` → `tickets` | 1 : N | `called_by_user_id`: attendant who called the ticket |
-| `totems` | per entity | Device registration for API auth; **no** ticket relationship |
-
-## Modeling Notes
-
-- **Account vs member:** `users` is the login account (Laravel Auth); `entity_memberships` is the user's link to the entity with role.
-- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
-- **Owner and circular FK:** `entities.owner_membership_id` points to the membership with `role = owner`. Since `entity_memberships.entity_id` references `entities`, the FK is circular — on bootstrap, create entity with `owner_membership_id` null, create owner membership, then fill the FK (or use deferrable constraint). Ownership transfer updates this FK and involved roles.
-- **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
-- **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
-- **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
-- **Ticket `code`:** displayable password (e.g., `A012`) shown on totem/TV; scope and format per queue/entity.
-- **Fairness:** 3-ticket priority fairness rule calculated in domain (queue state), no extra table.
-- **Separated finance:** `billing_accounts` (1:0..1 with entity) + `subscriptions` + `plans` isolate financial model. Entity without billing can be created and tested without payment configuration. `payment_options` defines cycle (MONTHLY/ANNUAL), method (PIX/CARD/BOLETO), discount and refund window. `payments` tracks individual charges with `due_date`, `paid_at`, `refund_deadline`. Asaas webhooks update `status` idempotently. `asaas_customer_id` in `billing_accounts`; `asaas_subscription_id` in `subscriptions`; `asaas_payment_id` in `payments`.
-- **Active subscription unique:** `billing_account_id` is UK in `subscriptions` (1:1); payment history in `payments`.
-- **Payment option:** `payment_options` can be preferred (`is_preferred`) and active (`is_active`). Discount (`discount_percent`) and refund window (`refund_window_days`) configurable.
-- **Payments:** `payments` tracks each charge generated by subscription; status synced with Asaas (PENDING, RECEIVED, REFUNDED, CANCELED, OVERDUE).
-- **Billing account:** `cpf_cnpj` stores fiscal data for invoice generation.
-- **Enums:** `role` (`admin`, `owner`, `employee`); `subscriptions.status`; `tickets.channel`; `tickets.status` — values in business rules.
-- **Unique constraints:** `billing_accounts (entity_id)`; `entity_memberships (entity_id, user_id)`; `queues (entity_id, slug)`; `queue_access (entity_membership_id, queue_id)`; `tickets (queue_id, code)` per issuance window; `payments (asaas_payment_id)`; `subscriptions (billing_account_id)` (1:1).
-- **Suggested indexes:** `(queue_id, status, priority, issued_at)` on `tickets`.
